WEBVTT

01:22.561 --> 01:27.380
RoboPrompt lets users steer robots with points, traces, or coarse directions.

01:28.118 --> 01:31.567
These corrections also provide data for policy improvement.

01:31.966 --> 01:35.295
A lightweight model drafts actions from human intent.

01:36.098 --> 01:38.356
The base policy then refines them.

01:38.768 --> 01:41.896
Phase I learns from 500 play trajectories,

01:41.988 --> 01:44.961
with prompt labels derived from the robot's motion.

01:46.068 --> 01:49.742
This turns sparse guidance into continuous action chunks.

01:51.468 --> 01:55.004
In Phase II, the base policy refines these action drafts

01:55.024 --> 01:59.327
through continuous denoising, producing precise, task-aware motion.

01:59.963 --> 02:04.438
Finally, time-weighted optimal transport selects high-quality rollout data.

02:05.212 --> 02:08.664
Training on this filtered data improves policy performance.
